      "description": "Watch Estoril Praia vs Famalicao highlights and goals from Primeira Liga on ReFooty: Football Highlights Hub. Match played on August 7, 2026. The energy of the Primeira Liga was on full display in a match where tactical discipline and individual skill took center stage. Estoril Praia and Famalicão faced off in a clash that promised high intensity, with both teams eager to claim dominance in a tightly contested fixture. Koutsias Strikes After VAR Review On August 7, 2026, the game opened with both sides testing each other's defensive resolve. It was Famalicão who found the breakthrough in the 32nd minute. A fluid attacking move saw Sorriso play a key pass to Gil Dias , whose assist allowed Georgios Koutsias to tap the ball home for an easy finish. The goal was initially put on hold for a VAR check, but after a brief period of suspense, the referee signaled that the goal stood, giving the away side the lead. Estoril's Resurgence and Begraoui's Leveler As the second half progressed, Estoril intensified their search for an equalizer, leading to a more physical contest that saw Ricard Sánchez enter the referee's book. Their persistence finally paid off in the 72nd minute. Tactical substitute Pedro Carvalho made an immediate impact, delivering a perfect ball to Yanis Begraoui , who clinicaly finished with his left foot to bring the hosts level and set up a frantic final period. Late Drama and Shared Points In the closing stages, both managers turned to their benches to find a winning spark. Famalicão introduced Umar Abubakar , who nearly snatched a late victory with a header that sailed just wide in stoppage time. Despite late pressure and a flurry of tactical substitutions including Tiago Brito and Oscar Aranda , neither side could find a decisive winner. The match concluded with 50% possession for each team, reflecting a balanced and hard-fought afternoon of football."
